  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a custom GLSL water surface on a 256×256 subdivided grid, 320 units wide. The vertex shader sums four sine waves and derives the normal from their gradient. The fragment shader adds a fresnel blend of body colour and sky reflection, and two-octave value-noise ripples that perturb the normal. It also adds a sun specular glint and distance fog toward the horizon colour. The sky is `sky.gradient` with a matching gradient hard-coded in the shader. The camera is a perspective camera 5 units above the water, looking toward the horizon. `uTime` drives the animation, and the shader outputs linear colour so the engine handles tone mapping. It sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` after `app.ready()`. Typecheck passes. I couldn't run `vite build` or view the scene, so the look is untested. The shader colours are my own tuning and the sky gradient colours are only approximately matched to the shader's.",
